<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

<!-- About page. The team members and their photos are fictional. -->
<template id="about" name="About">
    <t t-call="website.layout">
        <div id="wrap" class="oe_structure oe_empty">

            <!-- 1. Intro: dark band that runs into the next section through
                 the snippet's bottom shape. -->
            <section class="s_hero_about o_cc o_cc5 pt96 pb96" data-oe-shape-data="{'shape':'html_builder/Connections/20','colors':{'c5': 'o-color-4'},'flip':[], 'showOnMobile':true}" data-snippet="s_hero_about" data-name="Hero About">
                <div class="o_we_shape o_html_builder_Connections_20 o_shape_show_mobile" style="background-image: url('/html_editor/shape/html_builder/Connections/20.svg?c5=o-color-4');"/>
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="row align-items-end">
                        <div class="col-lg-7 pt24 pb24">
                            <p class="text-o-color-2 text-uppercase fw-semibold">About K'awiil</p>
                            <h1 class="display-2-fs">Lightning is the one force every culture has a god for.</h1>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-5 pt24 pb24">
                            <p class="lead">We build motorcycles that run on it. K'awiil Motors designs, assembles and finances electric motorcycles in San Francisco, California.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-12">
                            <div class="s_hr pt16 pb24" data-snippet="s_hr" data-name="Separator">
                                <hr class="w-100 mx-auto" style="border-top-width: 2px; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: var(--o-color-2) !important; opacity: 1;"/>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-12 pt24 pb24">
                            <img class="img img-fluid" src="/kawiil_website/static/img/about_workshop.jpg" style="width: 100% !important;" alt="Bright assembly workshop with Raijin frames on stands"/>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2. Story -->
            <section class="s_text_image pt112 pb112" data-snippet="s_image_text" data-name="Image - Text">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="row align-items-start">
                        <div class="col-lg-6 pt16 pb16">
                            <p class="text-o-color-1 text-uppercase fw-semibold">Our story</p>
                            <h2>From a Mission District garage to Thunderbird Road.</h2>
                            <p>Itzel grew up on the back of her father's motorcycle, and on her grandmother's stories from Yucatán about K'awiil, the Maya god of lightning. Years later, working as a battery engineer, she kept coming back to the same thought: the lightning in those stories was now the thing that could make motorcycles cleaner, quieter and faster.</p>
                            <p>In 2018 she started building a prototype in a rented garage in San Francisco's Mission District with Tomás Herrera, a race mechanic who had spent ten years tuning petrol superbikes and was ready for something new. Their first bike was rough, heavy and had a range of 40 miles. It was also quicker off the line than anything Tomás had ridden.</p>
                            <p>The name followed the idea. K'awiil gave the company its name, and every model since has been named after a lightning or thunder god from another part of the world: Raijin from Japan, Ukko from Finland, Indra from India. Different cultures, one force.</p>
                            <p>The biggest problem turned out not to be the bikes. Riders loved the test rides, then banks turned them down because they didn't know how to value an electric motorcycle. So in 2025 K'awiil started financing its own bikes. Arjun Mehta built the program so that riders apply online, get a decision quickly and ride away with a payment they planned for.</p>
                            <p>Today K'awiil designs, assembles and services every bike at its workshop on Thunderbird Road in the Dogpatch. Every model is built for one purpose: the ride should be the best part of your day.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-5 offset-lg-1 pt16 pb16">
                            <img src="/kawiil_website/static/img/about_story.jpg" class="img img-fluid mx-auto" alt="White electric adventure motorcycle on a stand in a workshop"/>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 3. Milestones -->
